#printing the output
print(value)
print(my-dict)
</textarea></div><p><strong>Output:</strong></p><div class="codeblock3"><pre>14
{'name': 'TpointTech', 'city': 'Noida'}
</pre></div><p><strong>5. Does pop() return the entire key-value pair?</strong></p><p>No, it only returns the value of the removed key. The key gets deleted from the dictionary automatically.</p><hr/><div class="nexttopicdiv"><span class="nexttopictext">Next Topic</span><span class="nexttopiclink"><a href="python-dictionary-values-method">Python dictionary values method</a></span></div><br> <div id="bottomnext"><a class="next" href="java-stringbuffer-delete-method" style="float:left">← prev</a> <a class="next" href="python-dictionary-values-method" style="float:right">next →</a></div><br/></br></td></tr></tbody></table></div><br/></div><div class="related-posts-container"><h2 class="h3">Related Posts</h2><ul class="related-posts-list"><li><a class="related-post-item" href="python-dictionary-fromkeys-method"><h3 class="h3">Python Dictionary fromkeys() Method</h3><p class="related-post-content">The dictionary fromkeys() method in Python returns the dictionary with key mapped to the value given in the &amp;#39;value&amp;#39; parameter. It does not change anything in the given dictionary; instead, it creates a new dictionary in the sequence of the specified values. Syntax: The following is the...</p><p class="reading-time"><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 4 min read <span class="arrow-position"><svg fill="currentColor" height="1.3rem" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewbox="0 0 512 512" width="1.3rem" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M295.6 163.7c-5.1 5-5.1 13.3-.1 18.4l60.8 60.9H124.9c-7.1 0-12.9 5.8-12.9 13s5.8 13 12.9 13h231.3l-60.8 60.9c-5 5.1-4.9 13.3.1 18.4 5.1 5 13.2 5 18.3-.1l82.4-83c1.1-1.2 2-2.5 2.7-4.1.7-1.6 1-3.3 1-5 0-3.4-1.3-6.6-3.7-9.1l-82.4-83c-4.9-5.2-13.1-5.3-18.2-.3z"></path></svg></span></p></a></li><li><a class="related-post-item" href="python-dictionary-setdefault-method"><h3 class="h3">Python Dictionary setdefault() Method</h3><p class="related-post-content">In Python, the setdefault() method is a dictionary meth